<title>USA: Georgia 900 MW coal unit seen up Saturday.</title>
<headline>Georgia 900 MW coal unit seen up Saturday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Georgia Power Co said it expects the 900 megawatt Scherer coal-fired power unit 2 to resume electrical output on Saturday following a brief maintenance outage.</p>
<p>The Juliette, Ga. unit was shut late Thursday or early Friday for planned maintenance, a Georgia Power spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Scherer's three other units, also rated at 900 megawatts each, were operating at full output, the spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Georgia Power, a subsidiary of Southern Co, is the operator of Scherer.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627</p>
</text>
